      "text": [
        " : كُنْتُ أَبِيعُ اَلسَّابِرِيَّ فِي اَلظِّلاَلِ فَمَرَّ بِي أَبُو اَلْحَسَنِ اَلْأَوَّلُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ رَاكِباً فَقَالَ لِي \"يَا هِشَامُ إِنَّ اَلْبَيْعَ فِي اَلظِّلاَلِ غِشٌّ وَ اَلْغِشُّ لاَ يَحِلُّ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith. - Hisham ibn Al-Hakam narrated:\n\"I used to sell Sabiri (a type of cloth) in the shade, and Abu Al-Hasan the First (as) passed by me while riding.\nImam (as) said to me: 'O Hisham, selling in the shade is deceit, and deceit is not permissible.'\""
        ]
      }
